{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "id": "kukhnya-s01e18-scene-19",
 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "Экономия на бармене  (Saving on the Bartender)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "kostya": "Костя",
  "nagiyev": "Нагиев"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Nagiyev's savings plan has reached the bar. He has found a way to economise on staff, and Kostya is the first to hear. Listen for how little time it takes.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Я просто делал свою работу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Мы экономим на всём.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Мы сэкономили на бармене.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Вы не можете меня уволить.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ты уволен, балбес.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Балбес, да?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Это очень несправедливо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ресторан в трудном положении.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Кто будет наливать напитки?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Это больше не твоя проблема.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Хорошо, я уйду сегодня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Вот и отлично.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Here's how the firing goes, word by word.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Я просто делал свою работу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I was just doing my job.' \"Svoyu\", my own, points back to \"ya\". \"Delal\", was doing, paints it as ongoing work.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Мы экономим на всём.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We're saving on everything.' You save on something: \"na\". After it, \"vsyo\", everything, becomes \"vsyom\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Мы сэкономили на бармене.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We've saved on the bartender.' The \"s-\" in \"sekonomili\" marks it as done. \"Barmen\" becomes \"barmene\" after \"na\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Вы не можете меня уволить.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You can't fire me.' Kostya says the polite \"vy mozhete\" to the owner, who says \"ty\" back.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ты уволен, балбес.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You're fired, idiot.' \"Uvolen\", fired, is a short form, so no 'are' is needed. \"Balbes\" is a blockhead.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Балбес, да?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'An idiot, huh?' A \"da?\" tacked on the end works like 'huh?' or 'is that so?'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Это очень несправедливо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'That's really unfair.' \"Nespravedlivo\" is \"ne\", not, plus \"spravedlivo\", fair, which shares a root with \"prav\", right.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ресторан в трудном положении.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The restaurant's in a tight spot.' \"Polozhenie\", situation, literally a position. \"V trudnom polozhenii\", in a difficult one.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Кто будет наливать напитки?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Who'll pour the drinks?' \"Budet nalivat\", will be pouring: a job that goes on. \"Napitki\", drinks, comes from \"pit\", to drink.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Это больше не твоя проблема.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'That's no longer your problem.' \"Bolshe ne\", 'more not': no longer. \"Problema\" is feminine, so your is \"tvoya\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Хорошо, я уйду сегодня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Fine, I'll leave today.' \"Uydu\", I'll leave: the \"u-\" means away. \"Segodnya\", today, is said \"sevodnya\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Вот и отлично.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Well, that's great.' \"Vot i otlichno\", 'so there, excellent': that settles it. Now the dismissal again, short and brutal.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Я просто делал свою работу.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Мы экономим на всём.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Мы сэкономили на бармене.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Вы не можете меня уволить.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ты уволен, балбес.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Балбес, да?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Это очень несправедливо.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Ресторан в трудном положении.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Кто будет наливать напитки?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Это больше не твоя проблема.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Хорошо, я уйду сегодня.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Вот и отлично.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Kostya has been dismissed in a few short sentences, and he takes it with surprising calm. \"Balbes\", blockhead, is rude but mild: Russians often say it half-jokingly. See you next time!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Пока!",
   "gap": 0.3
  }
 ],
